e (116). Four Future Retail bays (117, 122, 123, 128) each with new toilet rooms (119/120, 121, 124/125/126, 127) per bay. Riser section detail A-101 shows carpet finish on plywood underlayment on 18 GA metal deck with 6\\\" metal studs. 11 new work notes: MTL furring with 5/8\\\" GWB, clean and paint CMU, 1/2\\\" GWB, carpeted risers, new stoop and canopy, hi/low drinking fountain, exterior cladding TBD (R-9.5 min per 2018 VECC), plywood/carpet on metal deck, 6\\\" studs @ 16\\\" OC, diagonal bracing. ST-1 through ST-5 and W-1 through W-4 partition types referenced to A-501 (not rendered).\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sheet_number\": \"A-102\",\n        \"title\": \"REFLECTED CEILING PLAN\",\n        \"discipline\": \"architecture\",\n        \"source_file\": \"36 RESEARCH_PERMIT PLANS.pdf\",\n        \"date\": \"05/09/2022\",\n        \"reading_notes\": \"Reflected ceiling plan at 3/32\\\"=1'-0\\\" scale. Business/training area shows 2'x2' ACT (acoustical ceiling tile) grid throughout office/classroom/corridor/restroom areas. Retail bays show exposed ceiling / open to above (X hatching). Legend identifies two ceiling types: 2'x2' ceiling tile and exposed/open to above. Note on plan: 'LIGHTING AND MECHANICAL DIFUSSER AND GRILL LAYOUT TO BE SUBMITTED SEPERATELY' — confirming MEP drawings were a separate submittal package not included in this set. This is a significant finding: the permit set is architectural-only, and mechanical/electrical/plumbing design was not part of this drawing package.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sheets_not_rendered\": [\n      {\n        \"sheet_number\": \"A-103\",\n        \"title\": \"ROOF PLAN\",\n        \"source_file\": \"36 RESEARCH_PERMIT PLANS.pdf\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"sheet_number\": \"A-104\",\n        \"title\": \"(not confirmed — listed as A-103 and A-104 in drawing index on CS101 but index shows: LS101, AD101, A-101, A-102, A-103, A-104... A-401, A-501, A-601)\",\n        \"source_file\": \"36 RESEARCH_PERMIT PLANS.p